Corrected message:

Stop earlier shapes and text swapping z-order when a third is drawn

Each save hands the layer its full shape (or text) list oldest-first,
but the layer puts new objects at the bottom, so its existing slots
read newest-first. Matching the two by position put already-drawn
objects into each other's slots from the third one on. The existing
objects are now matched in reverse; new ones still go in at the bottom
in draw order. Adds a regression test.
